{
 "decision": "Promo owner feedback follow-up 2026-11-12: 'Talon's walking sprites now look blurry/soft compared to the rest.' noise_audit.py over all 281 drawn frames: the flat WALK frames have 35% of their body pixels isolated (RUN 31%), the same as WAIT (38%) and the sheet median (30%), against 11% for the flight set; the 31 px sheet before the rung measured the same, so the rescale did not add speckle, though its route-2 frames (walk-00..02, run-02) have softer edges. The walk and run loops were cleaned because a cycling loop makes per-frame speckle boil; the rest of the sheet was measured and left.",
 "method": "See walk_cleanup.py for the rules. Flats are rebuilt from source_rows (the installed pixels at add7f2fef5); patches are hand corrections x,y,index applied last. Slopes are re-derived from the cleaned flats; support is the distance along the slope normal from the hotspot to the lowest pixel of the frame being replaced, kept so ground contact does not move.",
 "hand_patches": "Eleven pixels on walk-00, walk-01 and walk-02 (rescale route 2), all feather-tip or glove-shadow grey to white: their cheek had been reduced to grey, and walk-03..07 draw it white with a grey edge. No other hand pixel; no patch crosses a material.",
